---- nonzero / flatnonzero / argwhere / where / count_nonzero / extract / compress
ok   nonzero returns indices in C order for C- and Fortran-ordered arrays (documented 'always ... row-major, C-style order')
ok   flatnonzero == nonzero(ravel) == flat C-order indices
ok   argwhere == transpose(nonzero) (rows of coordinates); 0-d argwhere shape (1, 0) / (0, 0)
ok   where(condition) with one argument == nonzero(condition)
ok   nonzero on floats: NaN and -0.0 count as nonzero / zero respectively; on bool; on strings (empty is zero)
ok   count_nonzero: total, axis=0, axis=1, tuple axis, keepdims
ok   count_nonzero 3-D with axis=(0, 2)
ok   count_nonzero on floats with NaN (nonzero) and on strings
ok   extract(cond, arr) == arr[cond] (C order) and == compress(ravel(cond), ravel(arr))
ok   extract with a non-boolean condition (nonzero = True)
ok   compress(axis=0) selects rows; axis=1 columns; axis=None flattens
ok   compress with a shorter condition truncates (documented)
ok   compress with a longer condition raises IndexError  (got IndexError)
